{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-30T21:08:45.824Z","data":{"text":"Done. Summary of the work:\n\n**Source changes**\n- `src/watcher/git-guard.ts`: `scopeViolations` now uses `scopeCoversPath(options.scope, file)` instead of `resolveScope`, so a deleted file is still covered by the scope entry naming it (exact or glob). The new-untracked-test and change-folder exemptions are untouched.\n- `src/core/run/task-commit.ts`: `verifiedCommitPaths` keeps every `scopedStatusPaths` result whether or not it exists; only the four change-folder records still go through `existingPaths`. Sorted and deduped.\n\n**New test** — `tests/scope-deletions.test.ts` drives `runWatcherCycle` in an osq worktree:\n1. A `tests.modify: true` task deletes `src/old.ts` (exact scope) and `tests/old.test.ts` (`tests/*.test.ts` glob); task is done, `osq: 001 task 1 verified` shows both `D` lines, worktree clean outside `.run/`, no `scope_violation`.\n2. A task deleting `src/out.ts` outside scope records a `scope_violation` naming it.\n\n**Verification**\n- `node --import tsx --test tests/scope-deletions.test.ts` — 2 passed.\n- `pnpm verify` — full suite + lint passed (after a biome format fix to the new test).\n\nResult written to `openspec/changes/126-scope-deletions/.run/results/1.md`."}}
